title: 'pallet-revive: add `burn` to the System precompile'
doc:
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    The System precompile gains `burn(uint256 amount)`. It removes `amount`, a balance with
    EVM decimals, from the spendable balance of the calling contract or account and from the total
    issuance. Held and frozen funds and the existential deposit are not spendable. When `amount`
    has a dust part the caller does not hold, one more spendable unit of the native currency is
    converted into dust first.

    The call reverts when the spendable balance of the caller is lower than `amount`, when
    `amount` is larger than the balance type of the chain can hold, when `msg.value` is not
    zero, or when the precompile is reached through a delegate call. In a static context it
    fails without revert data.
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Contracts can now reduce the total issuance. `System.burn` bypasses `Config::OnBurn`, which
    keeps receiving the gas rounding only, and a runtime cannot disable the function. No
    migration is needed.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
- name: pallet-revive-uapi
  bump: major
- name: pallet-revive-fixtures
  bump: minor
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
